1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,360
This smile is part living skin tissue and part robot.

2
00:00:06,019 --> 00:00:10,900
It's the product of a decade of research by scientists at the University of Tokyo.

3
00:00:11,960 --> 00:00:18,579
It may look a little eerie, but researchers say it could one day be used for testing cosmetics and medicine

4
00:00:18,579 --> 00:00:23,100
and is an important step in the quest to make more life-like robots.

5
00:00:23,859 --> 00:00:29,399
To create the smiling robot, scientists grew human cells into the shape of a face.

6
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:35,740
The smile is produced from embedded ligament-like attachments that pull it into a wide grin.

7
00:00:36,960 --> 00:00:40,020
Here's lead researcher Shoji Takesuchi.

8
00:00:41,939 --> 00:00:45,500
Until now, no one had figured out how to make the living skin move.

9
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:52,780
So I think by attaching these actuators and anchors, it became possible to manipulate living skin for the first time.

10
00:00:53,100 --> 00:00:55,679
This is a new technology that we developed.

11
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:06,060
Takesuchi says living tissue has a number of advantages over metal and plastic, such as skin's ability to repair itself.

12
00:01:06,420 --> 00:01:12,200
The hope is to add more features to the lab-grown skin, including a circulatory system and nerves.

13
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:21,599
Takesuchi says the work could potentially lead to safer testing for cosmetics and drugs, or be used to cover robots one day.

14
00:01:22,819 --> 00:01:26,760
One problem he still faces is the so-called uncanny valley.

15
00:01:27,420 --> 00:01:32,480
That's the unsettling feeling that comes when robots start to resemble humans a little too closely.

16
00:01:33,519 --> 00:01:36,500
Takesuchi says he hopes to overcome it.

17
00:01:38,060 --> 00:01:44,459
Various things have been talked about to reduce the creepiness, but I think one of the important matters is the materials.

18
00:01:46,359 --> 00:01:53,060
I think that making robots out of the exact same materials as humans, and having them show the same expressions,

19
00:01:54,819 --> 00:01:57,739
might be one key to overcoming the uncanny valley.

